_np = [['Collect examples from a normal day, such as email address, phone number, photo, delivery address, device identifier, location trace and customer number, and sort them by how easily they identify someone.', "Mark which items are especially sensitive, such as health, money or children's details, since they need stronger protection and a clearer reason to hold them."], ['Apply the habits of collecting only what you need, using it only for the stated reason, keeping it accurate, storing it briefly and keeping it safe.', 'Test each form field by asking what would go wrong if you did not collect it; if the answer is nothing, remove the field.'], ['List each data type with where it comes from, where it is stored, who can see it, who it is shared with and when it is deleted; aim for 10 rows to start.', 'Include informal places such as spreadsheets, chat messages, personal phones and paper files, since these are where leaks often begin.'], ['Score each data flow for likelihood and harm from 1 to 3, multiply, and tackle anything scoring 6 or more first with a named fix and date.', 'For new projects run a short checklist before starting: what data, why, who sees it, how long kept and what could go wrong for the person.'], ['Write notices in plain language at roughly a reading age of 12, covering what you collect, why, who receives it, how long you keep it and how to contact you.', 'Make consent a separate, unticked choice where it is needed, record the date and wording shown, and make withdrawing as easy as agreeing.'], ['Set a standard response time, such as 30 days at most, log the date every request arrives, and name one person who owns each step.', "Verify identity in proportion to the risk before releasing anything, and check that you are not exposing someone else's details in the same file."], ["Apply basics such as locked devices, encrypted laptops, limited access by role and removal of leavers' accounts on their last day.", 'Write a breach checklist: stop the leak, record what happened, assess the risk to people, notify those who must be told and note the lessons.'], ['Review the data map every six months and after any new tool or service, and update the notice whenever the practice changes.', 'Train staff for 20 minutes twice a year using real examples from your own office, and ask each person to name one change they will make.']]
C['mods'] = [(m[0], m[1], list(m[2])+_np[i], m[3], m[4], m[5]) for i, m in enumerate(C['mods'])]
C['intro_add'] = ["You will recognise ordinary details that identify a person and rank them by sensitivity, so you know which information deserves the strongest care.", "You will apply core privacy principles to a real form and remove fields you cannot justify, reducing what you hold and what could leak.", "You will build a data map covering sources, storage, access, sharing and deletion, including spreadsheets and phones where leaks often start.", "You will score each data flow for likelihood and harm and fix the highest items first, so limited time goes to the biggest risks.", "You will write a plain-language notice and a separate, recorded consent choice, so people understand and control what happens to their details.", "You will handle access, correction and deletion requests with a set deadline and a proportionate identity check, without exposing anyone else's data.", "You will apply basic safeguards and a breach checklist, so a lost laptop or misdirected email is contained and reported methodically.", "You will schedule regular map reviews and short staff refreshers, keeping privacy practice current as tools and habits change."]
